  "text": "The salt spray tasted like regret. Elias ran a gloved hand through the sand, the familiar grit a comfort against the ache in his chest. He\u2019d been doing this for thirty years, patrolling this stretch of coastline, a silent guardian against the indifferent grey. Every morning, regardless of the weather, he walked the same path, past the clustered dunes and bleached driftwood, past the rusted hulks of what used to be \u2013 remnants of a history swallowed by the sea. It was a lonely ritual, a penitice of sorts. \n\nHe wasn\u2019t a fisherman, not anymore. Hadn\u2019t been for a long decade. He simply maintained the pathways, cleared debris, ensured the access points were safe. People came, mostly tourists, snapping pictures of the endless horizon, of the wildness, oblivious to the quiet burden he carried. They sought solace in the immensity of the ocean, while he sought escape within it. A refuge from the echoes of his own decisions. \n\nThe wind picked up, a howling lament that rattled the loose stones under his feet and sent sknot of the sound of the story of his life, they were. Never mind this i, he, it? I was meant to. Those, they, why, and the noise? Forget it. \n\nHe paused at the crest of a dune, shielding his eyes against the wind, and scanned the water. The grey was darker today, bruised with under colour. The boats stayed in the harbour, sensible. He felt a familiar tightening in his gut. This wasn\u2019t just weather. Something was different. A stillness. A waiting. He tasted the salt again, the tang sharper now, carrying a metallic undertone.\n\nSuddenly, a sound cut through the wind's roar \u2013 a low, mournful fog whistle, faint but distinct. It wasn't the usual mourn of the harbour's safety beacon. This came from further out, a deeper, more resonant tone. It resonated not just in his ears, but in his bones, a vibration in the very ground beneath his boots. \n\nHe continued his walk then, his gaze drawn out to sea. The fog started to roll in, thick and silent, swallowing the horizon. Visibility dropped to near-zero. The ceaseless rhythm of the waves, which had been a constant companion, became muffled, obscured. It was like watching the world fade to a soft blur. \n\nHe reached the end of his patrol, the marker of a day\u2019s obligatory trudsal, the end of the sand that guides the vag of the, the\u2026 the patrol. Then, the fog rolled into his shadow. A quietness endured, unbroken by human noise. Everything went silent. \n\n\n\nThe fog clung to him, heavy and damp, and he found himself looking out into the grey expanse. The fog was almost blinding. He felt a strange calm settle over him, a stillness without any noise and with no sound, as an answer to his selfs. It was the kind of peace he hadn\u2019 \u09a4\u09be\u0981\u09b9\u09be\u09b0, who\u2019s? The feeling before the horizon? The space and stillness\u2026 the way it closes in?",
